\tag{fdip}
\title{A two-dimensional interacting continuum field}
\date{2026-11-09}

\p{The [interacting spatial chain](fdip-00GV) has positive
probabilities and [unitary Hamiltonian evolution](fdip-00H8).
A relativistic field also requires arbitrarily fine spatial resolution
and an unbounded region of spacetime. How can the same quartic
interaction survive both limits while retaining positivity and producing
a local field with a unique vacuum?}

\p{The finite [weighted Gaussian laws](fdip-00GH) are placed on fixed
spacetime squares with zero exterior values. The mesh is removed before
the square expands. The constructive limits of Guerra, Rosen and Simon
and Fröhlich supply the field; a finite-volume comparison with
Bauerschmidt and Dagallier supplies mixing at sufficiently small positive
coupling. Gaussian integration, Schwartz distributions and the
closed-form operator framework of \ref{fdip-00H2} are prerequisites.}

\p{The continuum construction uses
\citek{guerra1975euclideanII} and \citek{frohlich1974schwingerI};
the comparison uses \citek{bauerschmidt2024logsobolev}.}

